{"availability":"available","full":"BradyAJohnston/nodebpy","name":"nodebpy","description":"Build node trees in Blender more elegantly with code","category":"Developer tools","language":"Python","stars":130,"forks":6,"created":"2026-01-13T17:38:37Z","updated":"2026-10-18T09:45:25Z","license":"GPL-3.0","branch":"main","homepage":"https://bradyajohnston.github.io/nodebpy/","topics":["blender","blender-python","blender-scripts","geometry-nodes"],"demo":"https://bradyajohnston.github.io/nodebpy/","color":"#323057","ink":"#d6caff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-19T18:05:07.294Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-19T18:05:07.294Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-19T18:05:07.294Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-07T02:53:45.472Z","stars":113,"forks":6},{"at":"2026-10-09T03:37:14.335Z","stars":118,"forks":6},{"at":"2026-10-12T06:27:06.368Z","stars":119,"forks":6},{"at":"2026-10-18T11:29:10.250Z","stars":128,"forks":6},{"at":"2026-10-19T18:05:07.294Z","stars":130,"forks":6}],"technologies":["Python"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Build node trees in Blender more elegantly with Python code. Geometry Nodes, Shader Nodes and Compositor nodes are all fully supported, with type hints and IDE auto-completion throughout.","A text-based version of nodes should bring the convenience of writing code with IDE auto-completion, type hinting, with overall compactness and readability, while staying as close as possible to what building a node tree via the GUI feels like."],"features":["Every node is a typed class named after the node it creates — 'Random Value' becomes g.RandomValue() — and node subtypes are class methods: g.RandomValue.vector().","Trees are built inside a with g.tree(...): context; instantiating a node class adds it to the current tree, and the tree's interface is declared with tree.inputs. / tree.outputs..","Nodes are linked with the >> operator, which picks the most compatible socket pair automatically (much like Node Wrangler's Alt + Right Click drag) — or address sockets explicitly through the .i. / .o. accessors.","Python's arithmetic, comparison and boolean operators create the matching Math / VectorMath / Compare / BooleanMath nodes: g.Value(1.0) 2 + (0, 0, 1).","Existing node trees — including ones wired up by hand in the GUI — can be exported back to nodebpy source with topython()."],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/BradyAJohnston/nodebpy/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"bc204885a937d571adc5ab96eebe6460f99e62d84d8920779b3c923a3afa599a","extractedAt":"2026-10-19T18:05:07.390Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-19T18:05:07.390Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"Build node trees in Blender more elegantly with Python code. Geometry Nodes, Shader Nodes and Compositor nodes are all fully supported, with type hints and IDE auto-completion throughout.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/BradyAJohnston/nodebpy/blob/main/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[],"fingerprint":"bc204885a937d571adc5ab96eebe6460f99e62d84d8920779b3c923a3afa599a","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/BradyAJohnston/nodebpy/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-19T18:05:07.391Z"},"overviewRepoUpdated":"2026-10-18T09:45:25Z","readmeSnapshot":{"version":1,"status":"saved","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/BradyAJohnston/nodebpy/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-19T18:05:07.391Z","hash":"bc204885a937d571adc5ab96eebe6460f99e62d84d8920779b3c923a3afa599a","originalBytes":5132,"storedBytes":5132,"truncated":false},"lastDemoCheckedAt":"2026-10-19T18:05:07.294Z","subjects":["Animation & motion","Maths & algorithms"],"platforms":[],"classification":{"version":4,"method":"local_rules","category":"Developer tools","subjects":["Animation & motion","Maths & algorithms"],"evidence":[{"subject":"Animation & motion","source":"metadata","match":"Blender"},{"subject":"Maths & algorithms","source":"metadata","match":"geometry"}],"platformEvidence":[],"platformSupport":"author_metadata_not_runtime_tested","suggestedSubjects":["MCP servers & agents","3D & gr